From eaf059082f3a32eb895de8a8d0e1e550c9472d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:27:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][DV] The streams of a Dolby Vision stream group read
 from its entries, as FFmpeg 9.1 has them

FFmpeg 9.1 (libavformat 63.10) gives a stream group its entries
(AVStreamGroup.entries and nb_entries: streams or child groups) and
deprecates AVStreamGroup.streams and nb_streams until libavformat 64
(FF_API_STREAM_GROUP_ENTRIES). The index of the enhancement layer of a
layered video group (AVStreamGroupLayeredVideo.el_index) is an index into
the entries (demux.c and dump.c of 9.1); for a group of streams only, as
the Dolby Vision groups are, the entries are its streams in the same order.

The demuxer (the tracks of a Dolby Vision group, and the line of the log
of layers not joined) and CDVLayerMerge::Find() read the streams of a
group through StreamGroupStreams.h: the entries from libavformat 63.10 on,
the streams before; an entry that is a child group is no stream. Nothing
changes in what is read; the deprecated fields are no longer used, so
that a build against FFmpeg 9.1 has no warnings of them and the code goes
on building once libavformat 64 takes them away.
